 t..."},{"business_id":"GmXC3CBu172Bkb0c6RnO7w","review_id":"lq_ESWpzrID4Zfkw61sHzA","date":"2015-08-17T03:18:03","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9483147263526917,"text_excerpt":"This place is amazing. We were lucky enough to score a spot at the communal table last minute thanks to our concierge and boy am I glad we did. First off the view at the communal table is cool because you get to watch the expediter and many of the dishes being created. So I recommend that seat if you like to be in the action, although it's probably only good for a couple and not more people because you can't really converse then. The wine menu is extensive and they have it all set up on an iPad which is a great tool for figuring out what you want for the evening. Ok now the food, amazing! We had the turtle soup and bone marrow to start and both were fantastic. The turtle soup had almost a..."},{"business_id":"GmXC3CBu172Bkb0c6RnO7w","review_id":"9VnkPwEd62erQuaYA2oWNA","date":"2015-11-28T22:52:44","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9432352781295776,"text_excerpt":"We went in this dinner expecting this to be the best restaurant we would visit in New Orleans. We weren't wrong at all. They have a beautiful bar in the front, and gorgeous tables throughout the restaurant. The wait staff are all very attentive, knowledgable, and friendly. You can tell by looking around that they have so many workers constantly moving around and helping any table that needed anything. We started with the crab beignets. Each had a different sauce under them, and each were delicious. We all then had the death by gumbo. Gumbo stuff into a quail, and then sauce poured over the top. This dish was phenomenal and one of my favorites of the whole trip. I then had the braised pork..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"GmXC3CBu172Bkb0c6RnO7w","photo_id":"FYNZGpWEudDixGRDuBncXA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/FYNZGpWEudDixGRDuBncXA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8794111013412476},{"business_id":"GmXC3CBu172Bkb0